commit 89ac4ba1f6c350f34200d7cc22851d07eabb89c1
Author: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Aug 15 22:13:59 2026 -0500

    cpu : make decode and speculative verify batches bit-identical
    
    llamafile_sgemm rejected n < 2 ("only enable sgemm for prompt processing"),
    so decode (n_q = 1) attention matmuls ran the plain vec_dot kernel while
    speculative verify batches (n_q >= 2) ran tinyBLAS. The two kernels
    accumulate the F16 dot products differently (double-precision scalar tail
    vs F32 FMA chains), so logits diverged from the first token and MTP verify
    acceptance checks were unsound.
    
    Reject n <= 8 instead, routing every decode-scale batch (n_q 1..8) through
    the same vec_dot kernels; llamafile is kept for prefill (n_q > 8).
    
    Verified on gfx1201 (CPU build): batch-vs-seq 0/64 flips, max|d| = 0.0000
    for Qwen3.5-4B and Gemma4-12B, flash on/off, n_batch 1..5; server MTP
    byte-identical to no-spec.
    
    Assisted-by: pi

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/llamafile/sgemm.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/llamafile/sgemm.cpp
index 99b7d5afa..73e582acd 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/llamafile/sgemm.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cpu/llamafile/sgemm.cpp
@@ -3816,8 +3816,14 @@ bool llamafile_sgemm(const struct ggml_compute_params * params, int64_t m, int64
     assert(params->ith < params->nth);
 
     // only enable sgemm for prompt processing
+    // decode (n_q = 1) and speculative verify batches (n_q = n_draft+1) must run the
+    // same kernels: llamafile rejects n < 2, so verify batches (n_q >= 2) ran tinyBLAS
+    // while decode ran vec_dot, accumulating differently and breaking the
+    // batch-vs-seq bit-identity that speculative acceptance checks rely on.
+    // Route every decode-scale batch through the plain vec_dot path and use
+    // llamafile only for prefill (n_q > 8, i.e. beyond the speculative batch range).
 #if !defined(__MMA__)
-    if (n < 2)
+    if (n <= 8)
         return false;
 #endif
 
